  "diary": "The day moved from the gate of the Directorate to the bench in Lodhi Garden, and finally to the counter of Masterji. In the morning, the office was closed, a withdrawal of the universal behind its own weekend. I carried the file’s knot—the name Hegde misapplied to the body Hegel—into the cool air. Sunil’s chai on the plastic stool did not solve it, but it steadied the head. The true difficulty is that the record identifies a person by a name, and when the universal slips, the particular is displaced. I occupy this bungalow by the residue of an error, not by my own title. Hegde will come Monday to settle this with papers, not arguments. In the afternoon, Mrs. Kapoor corrected my language. I called her routine 'peace'; she called it a messy desk kept orderly. She was right. Habit is not the tranquil state I had labeled, but a disciplined repetition that prevents mental clutter. I have revised my view accordingly. The day ended with Masterji confirming the bandhgala is finished but 'settling.' He does not lie about time. I bought a notebook to outgrow my paper. The file waits for Monday; the body has walked seven kilometers and eaten dal makhani. The distinction between possession and title remains open, but the head is clear.",
  "revision_log": "The thesis regarding the nature of habit has been revised: it is now understood as a disciplined repetition that maintains order, rather than a state of peace. The distinction between possession and title remains unresolved pending Hegde’s arrival. No other theses moved.",
